###  https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001550
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001550> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                            <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000276> ;
                                                   rdfs:label "Julian Calendar"@en ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Solar Calendar System that has a regular Year of 365 24-Hour Days divided into 12 Months with a leap day added at the end of February every 4 Years such that the average length of a Julian Year is 365.25 Days."@en ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The Julian Calendar was proposed by Julius Caesar as a reform of the Roman Calendar, took effect on 1 January 46 BC, and was the predominant Calendar System in Europe until being largely replaced by the Gregorian Calendar."@en ;
                                                   <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001754> "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Julian_calendar&oldid=1063127575"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                   <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/InformationEntityOntology"^^xsd:anyURI .


